  "scenarioFormat": "the scenario format: steps, each a call with its input and its expected result; a servicing scenario also has a \"given\" (the in-memory ports' starting point) and a \"state\" (the ports' state after the steps)",
  "testing": [
    "# How the service is tested",
    "Each acceptance scenario calls an entry point of LoansApplication (SPEC.md section 2) with each step's input and compares",
    "the result, in canonical JSON, with the expected one, field by field. The call \"periods\" is",
    "LoansApplication.dueDates().periods(request); \"factors\" is LoansApplication.rateFactors().factors(query, calculation);",
    "\"schedule\", \"document\" and \"disclose\" are the methods of LoansApplication.quotes(). Canonical JSON: a record is an object",
    "with its components in declaration order (an implementation of a sealed interface also carries \"@type\", its simple name),",
    "dates are \"yyyy-mm-dd\", BigDecimal is a string compared by value and scale (\"12.30\" is not \"12.3\"), enums are by name, an",
    "absent nullable value is null, lists are arrays in order. About 20% of the scenarios are public: you see their failures in",
    "full. The others are hidden: you see how many pass.",
    "The servicing calls \"book\", \"disburse\", \"billDue\" and \"invoicePaid\" are the methods of LoansApplication.create(ports),",
    "over in-memory ports made from the scenario's \"given\" (one set per scenario; the call \"today\" sets their clock); after the",
    "steps the ports' state is compared with the scenario's \"state\" in the same canonical JSON.",
    "The migration calls \"legacyTerms\" and \"reconcile\" are the methods terms and reconcile of LoansApplication.migration(); their input",
    "is the legacy loan as its records ({\"request\", \"runControl\", \"currency\", \"schedule\", \"reject\"}, each record the characters of",
    "the legacy dataset's record, \"currency\" and \"reject\" null when absent), decoded by the generated LegacyCodec into a LegacyLoan."
  ],
  "pools": {
    "about": "The engine's scenario pools (FE 7.2 to 7.4): the SME's generators, each a main class of the SME project run in its folder (jvm: its JVM options; ${repo} and ${FCG} as in host.generators), in this order; pipeline.sh pools runs them",
    "sme": "sme",
    "generators": [
      {"main": "com.mlcpu.loans.sme.CalendarPool", "args": ["pool/calendar/candidates.jsonl", "../service/loans-acceptance/src/test/resources/scenarios", "../scenarios.json", "reports/calendar-pool.md", "12"]},
      {"main": "com.mlcpu.loans.sme.RatesPool", "args": ["../service/loans-acceptance/src/test/resources/scenarios", "../scenarios.json", "reports/rates-pool.md", "2", "pool/rates/candidates.jsonl", "pool/rates/candidates-edge-p12.jsonl", "pool/rates/candidates-edge-more.jsonl", "pool/rates/candidates-kit.jsonl", "pool/rates/candidates-probes.jsonl", "pool/rates/candidates-probes-rate05.jsonl"]},
      {"main": "com.mlcpu.loans.sme.TermsPool", "args": ["pool/schedule", "pool/terms/envelope.jsonl", "../service/loans-acceptance/src/test/resources/scenarios", "../scenarios.json", "reports/terms-pool.md", "6"]},
      {"main": "com.mlcpu.loans.sme.SchedulePool", "args": ["pool/schedule", "../service/loans-acceptance/src/test/resources/scenarios", "../scenarios.json", "reports/schedule-pool.md", "3", "150", "60"]},
      {"main": "com.mlcpu.loans.sme.DisclosurePool", "jvm": ["-Djava.util.concurrent.ForkJoinPool.common.parallelism=16"], "args": ["pool/disclosure/document-candidates.jsonl", "pool/schedule", "../service/loans-acceptance/src/test/resources/scenarios", "../scenarios.json", "reports/disclosure-pool.md", "pool/disclosure/disclose-candidates.jsonl", "3", "150", "60"]},
      {"main": "com.mlcpu.loans.sme.ServicingPool", "args": ["pool/schedule", "../service/loans-acceptance/src/test/resources/scenarios", "../scenarios.json", "reports/servicing-pool.md"]},
      {"main": "com.mlcpu.loans.sme.PrivilegedPool", "args": ["pool/privileged", "../service/loans-acceptance/src/test/resources/scenarios", "../scenarios.json", "reports/privileged-pool.md", "2"]},
      {"main": "com.mlcpu.loans.sme.MigrationPool", "args": ["legacy-books.json", "${repo}", "${FCG}", "pool/schedule/pool.json", "../service/loans-acceptance/src/test/resources/scenarios", "../scenarios.json", "reports/migration-pool.md"]}
    ]
  },
  "host": {
    "name": "OFBiz",
    "script": "../../tools/forward/ofbiz-host.sh",
    "profile": "environments/ofbiz-plugin.yaml",
    "bundle": "H-OFBIZ",
    "sme": "sme",
    "generators": [
      { "main": "com.mlcpu.loans.sme.OfbizPool", "args": ["pool/schedule", "../host/service-model.json", "../host/scenarios/pool", "1"] },
      { "main": "com.mlcpu.loans.sme.OfbizMigrationPool", "args": ["legacy-books.json", "${repo}", "${FCG}", "../host/scenarios",
        "plugins/loans/testdef/scenarios", "sample-p12-half_even", "rejects-p12-half_even"] }
    ],
    "digests": ["host/digests/ofbiz.md"],
    "facade": "host/ofbiz-facade.md",
    "context": ["LoansPortContext"],
    "scenarios": { "public": ["host/scenarios/smoke", "host/scenarios/pool/public"], "hidden": ["host/scenarios/pool/hidden", "host/scenarios/migration"] },
    "examples": ["ofb-r001", "ofb-0017"],
    "javaLevel": 17,
    "timeoutMinutes": 20,
    "testing": [
      "The service runs inside Apache OFBiz (the pinned release) as the plugin \"loans\" (plugins/loans). The plugin is generated from",
      "the service model: its entities (Loan, LoanScheduleLine, LoanServicingLine, LoanProduct), its services (quoteLoanSchedule,",
      "discloseLoan, bookLoan, disburseLoan, billDueLoanInstallments, recordLoanInvoiceStatus, ...), their SECA on setInvoiceStatus,",
      "and the Java behind them: each service builds the API command from its context, calls the service's engine (the jars in",
      "lib/) through LoansApplication.create(ports) with the ports the generated LoansPortsFactory builds, and returns the outcome.",
      "The engine reaches OFBiz only through those ports. Ids, LoanBook and Clock are generated; Ledger, Billing and",
      "FinancialAccounts are the holes: they put the loan into OFBiz's own accounting (payments, invoices, financial accounts),",
      "which then posts it to the general ledger. Each scenario runs the plugin's services in OFBiz (on OFBiz's demo data and",
      "the plugin's) and compares the rows OFBiz holds afterwards. About 30% of the scenarios are public: you see their failures",
      "in full. The others are hidden: you see how many pass."
    ],
    "contract": [
      "OFBiz's checkstyle, 0 violations: lines of at most 150 characters; 4-space indentation, no tabs; braces on every if, else,",
      "  for and while; final classes; private fields; @Override on interface methods; no unused or star imports; an operator that",
      "  wraps a line starts the next one; one statement and one variable declaration per line; a newline at the end of the file."
    ]
  }
}
